---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Learning path">
  <p class="eyebrow">Learn / DMS V0</p>
  <h1>Ask, define, experiment, interpret.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Use one fictional monitoring problem to connect engineering intent, structured definitions and qualified evidence.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><h2><a href={`${base}learn/01-engineering-intent/`}>From Engineering Intent to Evidence</a></h2><p>Start with an operator’s need, define a coverage criterion and interpret an executable model’s result.</p></li>
    <li><h2><a href={`${base}learn/02-engineering-information-models/`}>Engineering Information Models</a></h2><p>Then change one definition, validate its fields and relationships, and decide which evidence still applies.</p></li>
    <li><h2><a href={`${base}learn/03-digital-threads/`}>Digital Threads and Knowledge Graphs</a></h2><p>Follow typed relationships, distinguish definitions from execution context, and explain change impact.</p></li>
    <li><h2><a href={`${base}learn/04-executable-models/`}>Executable Engineering Models</a></h2><p>Inspect the discrete calculation, separate evaluation from geometry, and reproduce its output.</p></li>
    <li><h2><a href={`${base}learn/05-experimentation/`}>Experimentation and Trade-offs</a></h2><p>Control the comparison, interpret separate candidate runs, and identify missing decision evidence.</p></li>
    <li><h2><a href={`${base}learn/06-verification-evidence/`}>Verification and Engineering Evidence</a></h2><p>Inspect what executed, reconcile test success with requirement failure, and qualify the evidence.</p></li>
  </ol>
  <p>All six lessons retain one ideal circular sensor. They do not establish real-world sensing performance.</p>
</Layout>
<style>li { margin: 2rem 0; } ol { padding-left: 1.5rem; }</style>
